cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Does the Malaysian SnR method find better entries than chance? A codified test on crypto, gold and silver against matched random entries"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23537688
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Solano Paul"
    given-names: "Sean"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-20"
abstract: "Code, result tables, robustness checks and literature map for a codified test of Malaysian SnR (MSNR), a social-media support-and-resistance method, on Bitcoin, Ether, Solana, a gold-backed token, gold and silver at 5-minute to daily bars. Every strategy trade is compared with random entries that share its stop and target geometry, costs and trend direction; a 116,708-variant search is corrected for false discoveries, and a look-ahead error in limit-entry variants is documented and fixed."
keywords:
  - "support and resistance"
  - "technical analysis"
  - "random-entry benchmark"
  - "multiple testing"
  - "cryptocurrency"
  - "gold"
  - "retail trading"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bruhmoment2023-real/malaysian-snr"
